From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Birk Skyum <birk.skyum@pm.me>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 22:31:18 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] soc: qcom: aoss: Fix the prevent_aoss_sleep message

The AOP keeps the AOSS out of sleep on {class: aoss_slp, res: sleep,
val: disable}. The prevent_aoss_sleep debugfs entry sends "res: sleep:
%s" without the val key, and maps Y, which asks to prevent sleep, to
"enable".

On a Samsung Galaxy Book4 Edge 14 (X1E-80-100), writing either Y or N
to the entry left the AOSD residency at 97 to 98 % of a suspend, while
the message above kept it at 0. Send that message, with "disable" for
Y and "enable" for N.

Fixes: d51d984c5525 ("soc: qcom: aoss: Add debugfs interface for sending messages")
Link: https://github.com/omacom/omarchy/discussions/15860#discussioncomment-19640176
Signed-off-by: Birk Skyum <birk.skyum@pm.me>
---
 drivers/soc/qcom/qcom_aoss.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/qcom/qcom_aoss.c b/drivers/soc/qcom/qcom_aoss.c
index 259c41f..a4ec434 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/qcom/qcom_aoss.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/qcom/qcom_aoss.c
@@ -498,7 +498,7 @@ struct qmp_debugfs_entry {
 
 static const struct qmp_debugfs_entry qmp_debugfs_entries[QMP_DEBUGFS_FILES] = {
 	{ "ddr_frequency_mhz", "{class: ddr, res: fixed, val: %u}", false },
-	{ "prevent_aoss_sleep", "{class: aoss_slp, res: sleep: %s}", true, "enable", "disable" },
+	{ "prevent_aoss_sleep", "{class: aoss_slp, res: sleep, val: %s}", true, "disable", "enable" },
 	{ "prevent_cx_collapse", "{class: cx_mol, res: cx, val: %s}", true, "mol", "off" },
 	{ "prevent_ddr_collapse", "{class: ddr_mol, res: ddr, val: %s}", true, "mol", "off" },
 };
